  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="bb455428-3be9-4223-b854-6aad6be555c1" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7a3f6355-50d8-4553-969c-c2510b2fabfc" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph defined by \(y=(x−3)^2+2\)?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 3. The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex is found by using the squared term of the vertex form. The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is 3.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a890445c-625a-426a-9e78-080b549637d9" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="2">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph defined by \(y=(x−3)^2+2\)?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 2. In vertex form, the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex is the constant. The value of the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is 2.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
